2026-10-09T18:51:52.4089727Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4090750Z         <b>0.4.27</b> � cleared the 2 deprecated-API usages the Marketplace verifier
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4091810Z         flagged (now <code>URI.toURL()</code> + a combo-box dialog), so the plugin
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4096036Z         stays compatible with future IntelliJ releases.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4176144Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4229073Z         <b>0.4.26</b> � fix: no more false "???? cc CLI" when <code>cc</code> IS
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4309871Z         installed. The version probe timeout went 5s ? 12s (cold starts), and since
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4433445Z         <code>cc</code> is also the C compiler's name, the plugin now resolves the
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4512810Z         binary with fallback (<code>cc ? chainlesschain ? clc ? clchain</code>) and
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4794166Z         uses it for the chat spawn and every probe.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4829231Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4877836Z         <b>0.4.25</b> � the agent can actually ask you a question:
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4879036Z         <code>ask_user_question</code> now pops a dialog (single-choice / multi-select
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4891845Z         checkboxes / free-text input) so the agent can clarify instead of guessing.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4958648Z         Requires <code>cc</code> ? 0.162.95.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4959242Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.4976788Z         <b>0.4.24</b> � fix: a graceful "couldn't ask in the panel" degradation no
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5017185Z         longer renders as a scary <b>? ask_user_question</b> failure.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5018492Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5021003Z         <b>0.4.23</b> � new <b>? LLM ? ?? cc ??�</b> menu item (check on demand),
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5023568Z         plus a clear hint when the <code>cc</code> CLI isn't installed.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5033721Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5034795Z         <b>0.4.22</b> � you're now told when a newer <code>cc</code> CLI is published
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5044201Z         on npm, so you don't silently miss new features.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5046284Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5048642Z         <b>0.4.21</b> � fix: reconfiguring the LLM now restarts the running chat so it
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5067160Z         picks up the new provider/model/key (no more "?????? / ??????").
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5073188Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5074565Z         <b>0.4.20</b> � new <code>/review</code> command: review your uncommitted git
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5081852Z         diff right from the chat (matches the VS Code panel).
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5082631Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5088384Z         <b>0.4.19</b> � fix: the suggested vision model now matches the CLI's
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5114645Z         actual default (<code>doubao-seed-2-0-lite-260215</code>) instead of an
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5138026Z         older snapshot, so the prefilled value equals what
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5179437Z         <code>cc agent --image</code> uses.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5186402Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5200049Z         <b>0.4.18</b> � dedicated image-recognition (vision) model entry: the
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5201250Z         <b>? LLM</b> button is now a small menu (configure full LLM <i>or</i> just
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5202740Z         the vision model), plus a <b>Tools ? Configure Vision Model</b> action.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5204301Z         Set <code>llm.visionModel</code> without re-running the whole wizard or
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5205358Z         re-typing your API key; blank reverts to the text model.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5206390Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5208215Z         <b>0.4.17</b> � first-run nudge: when no LLM provider is configured yet,
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5209443Z         the chat panel now shows a dim hint pointing at the <b>? LLM</b> button
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5210550Z         instead of staying blank until the first turn fails with a 401 (VS Code
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5211456Z         onboarding parity).
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5212077Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5213081Z         <b>0.4.16</b> � chat panel LLM UX: (1) paste screenshots � Ctrl/Cmd+V an
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5215161Z         image to attach it to your next message (vision); (2) a <b>? LLM</b>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5216520Z         quick-entry button by Send opens the provider/model wizard, and auth
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5217931Z         failures (401/403/missing key) now hint at it; (3) the wizard can set a
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5219383Z         separate <b>image-recognition (vision) model</b> � text and vision models
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5220266Z         no longer have to be the same.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5221058Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5222959Z         <b>0.4.15</b> � multi-line chat composer: the input now wraps across
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5225594Z         lines � <b>Enter</b> sends, <b>Shift+Enter</b> adds a newline (VS Code
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5226445Z         parity).
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5227773Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5228835Z         <b>0.4.14</b> � extended-thinking reasoning (with <code>/think</code>) now
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5232916Z         streams into the transcript dimmed/italic, set apart from the answer
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5234013Z         (VS Code parity).
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5234436Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5235236Z         <b>0.4.13</b> � Markdown rendering in the chat transcript: fenced/inline
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5236316Z         <code>code</code> (monospace) and <b>bold</b> now render instead of raw
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5237242Z         markers (VS Code parity). Streaming stays plain, then snaps to styled.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5238363Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5239540Z         <b>0.4.12</b> � "Fix with ChainlessChain" intention: on an error/warning
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5240620Z         line, Alt+Enter offers a quick-fix that seeds the chat with a fix request
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5241546Z         scoped to that file + those problems (VS Code parity).
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5242227Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5242999Z         <b>0.4.11</b> � slash-command autocomplete: typing <code>/</code> at the
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5243532Z         start of the chat input pops a chooser of the panel's commands
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5244760Z         (<code>/new</code>, <code>/compact</code>, <code>/think</code>, �),
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5245534Z         filtered as you type (VS Code parity).
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5246495Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5247273Z         <b>0.4.10</b> � fix: wrap the diff-review document reads
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5248204Z         (<code>openDiff</code>/<code>openMultiDiff</code>) in a read action.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5249595Z         Since 2026.2 the EDT no longer grants implicit read access, so building
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5251066Z         the diff threw "Read access is allowed from inside read-action only" on
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5252034Z         2026.2+. No behavior change on 2025.x.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5252580Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5253411Z         <b>0.4.9</b> � fix: the chat tool window now deterministically uses the
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5254435Z         LLM provider you configured (<code>cc config</code> / Configure LLM),
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5255462Z         reading <code>~/.chainlesschain/config.json</code> and passing it
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5256556Z         explicitly to <code>cc agent</code> � no more spurious
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5257518Z         <code>Anthropic error: 401</code> when another provider is configured.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5258300Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5259150Z         <b>0.4.8</b> � <code>/compact</code> in the chat tool window (Claude-Code
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5260224Z         IDE parity): trims the live conversation history between turns (no extra
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5261174Z         LLM call) and reports the tokens saved. Mirrors the VS Code 0.31.0
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5261933Z         feature.
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5262396Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5263252Z         <b>0.4.7</b> � cleared the remaining API-compatibility flags the Plugin
2026-10-09T18:51:52.5264282Z         Verifier reported on 2026.x: the @-mention list renderer no longer uses a
